Retro graph (axes, tick labels, axis titles)
Font: Courier New
Set in retro_manim_graph/_config_data.py as the default "font_family": "Courier New".
The scene’s FONT_FAMILY is set by get_default_class_config() in retro_configuration.py to "Courier New", and construct_retro_style_scene uses that for axis labels and axis titles (e.g. “X TRAIT”, “Y TRAIT”, “FITNESS”).

Optimized Lamarckian info panel
Font: Manim default
The panel is built with Text(..., font_size=18, color=BLACK, ...) with no font= argument, so it uses Manim’s default font (often something like Sans-Serif or the default Text font), not Courier New.

To run this on Windows from project root (location-agnostic):
.\manim.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m manim -qh --disable_caching "visualizationtool/lamarck_visualizations/6optimized_lamarckian_functions.py" SixOptimizedLamarckianFunctions -s
